  "title": "B-Roll: Coast Guard, animal rescue teams to transport pregnant manatee to Florida following rescue from cold Massachusetts waters",
  "description": "A U.S. Coast Guard HC-144 Ocean Sentry air crew from Air Station Cape Cod arrives with a pregnant manatee at Orlando International Airport, Tuesday, Oct. 18, 2016. The manatee was rescued from the waters of Falmouth, Massachusetts and transported to SeaWorld where animal rescue teams and veterinarians will provide care until she is ready to be released to her natural Florida habitat. (U.S. Coast Guard video by Petty Officer 3rd Class Nicole J. Groll and Petty Officer 2nd Class Ashley J. Johnson)",
